Nova Worker — Changelog
=======================

## [Beta-0.0.1] - 2026-10-08

First public release of Nova Worker.

### Panel

- Rebranded the whole panel to Nova Worker (title, logo alt, manifest, footers, demo data).
- Single-file admin panel: `Panel/admin/index.html`.
- Simplified dashboard: the quick-links and recent-activity cards are gone; the cards are always expanded (no collapse button).
- About card now shows the panel version `Beta-0.0.1` and the release date `Aban 1405`.
- The panel version label follows the highest version it finds: it reads the Worker's `/version` and the `Version` constant from the GitHub source, so a newer Cloudflare deployment or a newer GitHub release is reflected without editing the panel.
- Persian (RTL), English and Russian, switchable from the sidebar and remembered in the browser.
- Light theme only, inline SVG icons, no emoji.
- Login and install pages rebuilt in the same visual language.
- `Panel/index.html` is an entry page: on the static host it asks for the Worker domain and remembers it, elsewhere it forwards to `/admin`.
- Demo data, subscription sample and version file cleaned up for the new brand.
- Sessions end after 30 minutes without activity or as soon as the browser closes. The panel shows a 3-second countdown, then signs out and returns to the login page with a short notice.
- The dashboard no longer shows the status and quick-access cards; only the network and latency cards remain.
- The random IP count in «Preferred IP source» can now be set from 1 to 999 (it was capped at 99); a value stored at the old cap of 99 is shown as 999 and saved as 999.
- First login shows a one-time user-mode popup with two choices: beginner (personal/family use, about 4 users) and advanced (special settings, more than 5 users). The choice is saved in the Worker config KV as `PanelMode` (`"beginner"` or `"advanced"`), so it is asked only once and applies to every browser.
- Beginner mode keeps only Dashboard, Links, Network settings (Subscription basics, Preferred IP source, Protocol & transport) and About; the other nav items and cards are hidden. Advanced mode shows the full panel.
- About has a "Change user mode" card whose button always points to the other mode ("Switch to beginner" / "Switch to advanced"); the new choice is written back to the Worker KV (`PanelMode`) and never changes subscriptions or node settings.
- The first-run popup cannot be dismissed with Escape or a backdrop click, so a mode is always chosen.
- The subscription converter no longer downloads its preset lists from remote Chinese JSON files. The SubConverter backend list, the Clash rule (SUBCONFIG) presets and the path-template presets are now built into the panel with English labels, so the converter works even when GitHub is filtered. The generated URLs are unchanged.

### Worker

- Default panel address is `https://nova-panel.github.io`; `PANEL_URL` (variable or install setting) and the `ASSETS` binding override it.
- Panel static files (logo, manifest, QR script, Leaflet, fonts) are proxied through the Worker domain, so the panel renders correctly at `/admin`, `/login` and `/install`.
- When the panel cannot be reached, the Worker answers with a localized Nova Worker page instead of the upstream Chinese page.
- JSON error messages returned to the panel are in English.
- Panel responses are cached at the Cloudflare edge (HTML 5 minutes, static assets 1 hour), so switching between `/admin`, `/login` and `/install` no longer waits for GitHub Pages every time. Measured: 1.2 s cold → 4 ms warm.
- Panel data routes (`config.json`, `log.json`, `check`, `getADDAPI`, `getCloudflareUsage`) are never cached.
- Panel paths are normalized before fetching, so hosts that redirect `/install` → `/install/` do not cost an extra round trip.
- Admin sessions use a session cookie (no `Max-Age`) plus a server-side issue time: closing the browser or 30 minutes without activity forces a new login. `/admin` always requires a valid session; data routes answer `401` with `{success:false,error:'unauthorized',reason}`.
- Generated nodes are named `Nova Worker-Free service 1`, `Nova Worker-Free service 2`, … in the panel link and in the local subscription.
- Remaining upstream identifiers are gone: subscription user-agents and the subscription profile name now use `Nova Worker` and `https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker`.
- The Worker reports its public version `Beta-0.0.1` from `/version`; the build timestamp stays in `Build` for the subscription user-agent.

### Performance

- Vazirmatn is now self-hosted at `Panel/fonts/vazirmatn-var.woff2` (OFL, one variable file for weights 100–900) with `font-display: swap` and a preload hint. The render-blocking `fonts.googleapis.com` stylesheet is gone, which was the main reason pages stalled in Iran.

### Links

- Panel source: https://github.com/Nova-Panel/nova-panel.github.io
- Worker source: https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker
